API-15: rescale a gage's current rainfall when its scale factor is changed

recordRate() applies the scale factor when a record becomes current, so the
current record's rate (st_rain) keeps the old factor after
swmm_gage_set_scale_factor(), and a co-gage, which divides the primary's
rainfall by its new factor, gets a wrong value until that record has passed.
Multiply st_rain by new/old factor in the setter, so the new value "takes
effect on the next timestep" as the header documents.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-15_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp b/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp
index daf90cf..d92f748 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/openswmm_gages_impl.cpp
@@ -229,7 +229,11 @@ SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_gage_set_scale_factor(SWMM_Engine engine, int idx, doub
     if (factor <= 0.0) return SWMM_ERR_BADPARAM;
     auto& ctx = to_engine(engine)->context();
     CHECK_INDEX(idx >= 0 && idx < ctx.n_gages());
-    ctx.gages.scale_factor[static_cast<std::size_t>(idx)] = factor;
+    const auto uidx = static_cast<std::size_t>(idx);
+    // the current record's rate (st_rain) was computed with the old factor
+    if (uidx < ctx.gages.st_rain.size())
+        ctx.gages.st_rain[uidx] *= factor / ctx.gages.scale_factor[uidx];
+    ctx.gages.scale_factor[uidx] = factor;
     return SWMM_OK;
 }
 
